<title>SPAIN: Spain's Santander cuts prime 25 bp to 7.25.</title>
<headline>Spain's Santander cuts prime 25 bp to 7.25.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Santander said on Tuesday it cut its prime rate by 25 basis points to 7.25 percent.</p>
<p>The move followed the Bank of Spain's decision to lower its key money market to 5.50 percent from 5.75 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
